From dbe8ab8db9480bde02da584de3cabd92108d34e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Canepa <l.canepa@aequitax.pro>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:26:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mitgliedschaft): the fee tables fit a phone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On a phone the three fee tables ran past the right edge of the screen: the
fee column read "CHF 2" and "Davon Lizenz" was gone entirely. The wrapper
scrolled, but nothing hinted at it. Cause: the grid items (.fee-col,
.fee-block) default to min-width:auto, and the tables' min-content width —
nowrap headers, nowrap amounts, 24px cell padding — exceeded the 364px
track, so the whole column widened past the viewport.

- Grid items get min-width:0 so a table can never widen its column.
- Cell padding, alignment and the amount's font-size move out of the inline
  styles into the page stylesheet, where a phone breakpoint can tighten them
  (below 640px: smaller cells, 1rem amounts, headers may wrap).
- Below 480px the volleyball table stacks each row: category on top, "Beitrag"
  and "Davon Lizenz" on a row beneath with their column label (repeated
  inside the cells as a .fee-label span, translated by data-i18n, hidden
  elsewhere). Three columns left the German categories ~120px and broke
  "Mittelschüler:innen" and "Fachhochschulen" mid-word.
- Category cells hyphenate before an overflow-wrap:anywhere last resort.

Verified at 360/375/412/1280px in DE and EN: no table wider than its track,
no mid-word breaks, desktop unchanged. Unit suite and the layout,
accessibility, i18n and site-text e2e specs pass on desktop and mobile.

Changelog 1.28.1 (CHANGELOG.md, feedback page DE + EN).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
